   "source": [
    "en_vowels = [\"a\", \"e\", \"i\", \"o\", \"u\"]   # list of english vowels\n",
    "en_words = [\"banana\", \"splash\", \"strengths\"]\n",
    "\n",
    "for w in en_words:\n",
    "    print(\n",
    "        \"word:\", w, \n",
    "        \"-- cv pattern:\", cv_pattern(w, en_vowels), \n",
    "        \"-- syllables:\", syllabify(w, en_vowels)\n",
    "    )"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "34e74cdd",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "-   The word \"banana\" is correctly parsed by the functions, but \"splash\" and \"strengths\" are not. What goes wrong is that the other words are have the coda consonants cut off because the `syllabify()` function parses syllables at consonants. It never goes wrong for Hawaiian because Hawaiian syllables never have codas. This tells us that English syllables have less restrictive structure, especially in its codas.\n",
    "\n",
    "## Challenge (Optional): Diphthongs {#challenge}"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 12,
   "id": "f6fd7d63",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "[{'word': 'kai', 'syllables': 'ka.i', 'syllables_diphthong': 'kai'}]\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "def syllabify_diphthongs(word, vowels=hi_vowels, diphthongs=[\"ai\", \"ae\", \"ao\", \"au\", \"ei\", \"eu\", \"oi\", \"ou\", \"iu\"]):    # default in Hawaiian, change vowels value for other languages, also: hi_vowels is defined in lin301.py\n",
    "    syllable = \"\"\n",
    "    result = []\n",
    "    previous = \"\" # stores previous letter\n",
    "\n",
    "    for i in word:\n",
    "        if is_vowel(i, vowels) and previous + i in diphthongs:\n",
    "            result[-1] += i\n",
    "            previous = i\n",
    "        elif is_vowel(i, vowels):\n",
    "            syllable += i\n",
    "            result.append(syllable) # adds string of syllable to result as list item\n",
    "            syllable = \"\"   # clears syllable string so it is ready for next syllable\n",
    "            previous = i\n",
    "        else:\n",
    "            syllable += i\n",
    "            previous = i\n",
    "    return result\n",
    "\n",
    "hi_syllables_diphthongs = [\".\".join(syllabify_diphthongs(w)) for w in hi_df[\"word\"]]\n",
    "\n",
    "syllable_differences = []\n",
    "i = 0\n",
    "for w in hi_df[\"word\"]:\n",
    "    if hi_df.loc[i][\"syllables\"] != hi_syllables_diphthongs[i]:\n",
    "        syllable_differences = [{\n",
    "            \"word\": w, \n",
    "            \"syllables\": hi_df.loc[i][\"syllables\"], \n",
    "            \"syllables_diphthong\": hi_syllables_diphthongs[i]\n",
    "        }]\n",
    "    i += 1\n",
    "\n",
    "print(syllable_differences)"
   ]
  }
